<figure id="S3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.08572v1/methodquxian.png" id="S3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/79;" width="429" height="79" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 5</span>: </span><span id="S3.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">We evaluate the performance of four foundational motor skills: <span id="S3.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Walking, Running, Standing, and Sitting</span>, after 50w training steps. The dashed lines in the learning curves qualitatively represent the reward thresholds associated with the successful execution of each skill.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.08572v1/compare1.png" id="S3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/136;" width="476" height="136" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 6</span>: </span><span id="S3.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">In comparison with TD-MPC2, Green shaded areas highlight the superior performance of <span id="S3.F6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours</span>, whereas red regions indicate limitations observed in baseline algorithms.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To operationalize the composition operator <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, we propose an IRM that synthesizes motor primitives through a learnable routing network <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> expert policies <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and the VLM-provided semantic guidance <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, the routing network <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))</annotation></semantics></math> maps the current observation <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to a weight distribution <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The composition is defined as:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{mix}}(s)=\mathcal{F}_{\phi}(\{\pi_{i}(s)\}_{i=1}^{K};\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\cdot\pi_{i}(s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{mix}}(s)=\mathcal{F}_{\phi}(\{\pi_{i}(s)\}_{i=1}^{K};\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\cdot\pi_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=[\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))]_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=[\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))]_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the weight assigned to the <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th expert. To achieve autonomous task execution, we propose a hierarchical semantic distillation pipeline:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task-Level Semantic Prior (Coarse Alignment).</span>
We derive task-level relevance scores <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> from the VLM based on the task description <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The router aligns with this global guidance to distill foundational task semantics:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}(\phi)=\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))\,\|\,\mathbf{w}_{v})-\beta\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\phi})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}(\phi)=\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}(\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))\,\|\,\mathbf{w}_{v})-\beta\mathcal{H}(\pi_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the zero-shot expert relevance inferred by the VLM for task <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy regularization coefficient, and <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the policy entropy. This objective determines which experts are globally relevant for a given task, providing essential semantic grounding.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Demonstration-Level Behavioral Refinement (Fine Alignment).</span>
To capture temporal composition, we use few-shot demonstrations <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. The VLM extracts a demonstration-conditioned prior <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{demo}}(\mathbf{w}|D)\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{demo}}(\mathbf{w}|D)\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects expert usage statistics observed in trajectories. The router is optimized via:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}(\phi)=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{T}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))\,\|\,P_{\text{demo}}(\mathbf{w}|D)\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}(\phi)=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{T}}}\left[\mathcal{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\phi}(\mathbf{w}|s,\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))\,\|\,P_{\text{demo}}(\mathbf{w}|D)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Unlike <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which provides coarse guidance, <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math> refines the router to match the temporally consistent expert composition statistics found in demonstrations <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ III-D VLM-Guided Semantic Routing for Expert Composition ‣ III Methodology ‣ MetaWorld-X: Hierarchical World Modeling via VLM-Orchestrated Experts for Humanoid Loco-Manipulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unified Training Objective.</span>
The final objective integrates coarse task semantics and fine-grained behavioral priors into a unified hierarchical supervision framework:</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{IRM}}(\phi)=\lambda(t)\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}(\phi)+\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}(\phi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>IRM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>task</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{IRM}}(\phi)=\lambda(t)\cdot\mathcal{L}_{\text{task}}(\phi)+\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(t)=\lambda_{0}\eta^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(t)=\lambda_{0}\eta^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a time-decaying guidance weight, with <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as the initial weight, <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> as the decay rate, and <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the training iteration. This schedule facilitates a transition from VLM-guided bootstrapping (high <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(t)</annotation></semantics></math>) to demonstration-based behavioral refinement (dominant <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math>). Task-level alignment provides semantic grounding, while few-shot transfer refines behavioral composition. Together, they form a hierarchical semantic distillation mechanism for expert routing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">III-E</span> </span><span id="S3.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inference Procedure</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At inference time, the IRM module functions as a low-latency routing network that synthesizes motor primitives in real-time. Given the cached task guidance <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math> and the current observation <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the routing network produces the optimal weight distribution <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}=\pi_{\phi}(s_{t},\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}=\pi_{\phi}(s_{t},\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}))</annotation></semantics></math>, enabling the composition operator to generate the final action:</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}=\mathcal{F}_{\phi}(\{\pi_{i}(s_{t})\}_{i=1}^{K};\mathbf{w}_{t})=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{t,i}\cdot\pi_{i}(s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}=\mathcal{F}_{\phi}(\{\pi_{i}(s_{t})\}_{i=1}^{K};\mathbf{w}_{t})=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{t,i}\cdot\pi_{i}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This avoids redundant VLM queries during control, ensuring the framework maintains high-frequency execution for complex loco-manipulation tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiment</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate our approach, we conduct comparison experiments on both fundamental locomotion tasks and complex locomotion and manipulation tasks from the Humanoid-bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, ablation study.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Comparison Experiments of Policy Learning</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental Setup.</span> 
Our primary objective is to leverage expert policies for basic skills to accelerate learning in complex locomotion and manipulation tasks. To this end, we construct eight minimally orthogonal robotic skill experts: <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Stand, Walk, Run, Sit, Carry, Reach, and Crawl</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Performance comparison on locomotion tasks (Success Rate / 10). <span id="S4.T2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours</span> outperforms all baseline RL and model-based algorithms.</figcaption>
